text:
@Niquoa Saying AI is completely useless or 'anti-human' is just being dramatic.
It's already fixing computer code, reading giant documents in seconds, and translating languages instantly.
You don't have to believe the wild sci-fi hype to see that it’s actually useful right now.

@L7hf3jYou're mixing things up, the internet being hard to crash isn't the same as us not depending on it.
That's like saying because a car has a spare tire and doesn't break easily, you don't actually need a car to drive to work.
Just because the internet is built to survive broken connections doesn't mean our economy can survive without it.

@FaqiribnAqeel A word analogy is a word that is an analogy. It can be a noun. It often is. Is a branch _only_ of a tree? etc.

The point is talking of illusions and truth followed by an analogy as support for your prediction is really ironic and fun to point to.

Cheers.
